## KratosOS persona isolation policy for Qubes OS (qrexec, 4.1+ format).
##
## Installed to dom0 as /etc/qubes/policy.d/30-kratos.policy. It runs BEFORE
## the default 90-* policies, so these denies win. Every qube that holds the
## persona carries the tag 'kratos-persona' (set by the Salt formula). The
## rule is simple and total: nothing crosses out of a persona qube.
##
## This is the Qubes-native version of KratosOS's "nothing leaves the persona"
## rule, enforced by dom0 (the trusted base) instead of by the host kernel.

## ---- Clipboard: no copy OUT of a persona qube, to anywhere ----
qubes.ClipboardPaste  *  @tag:kratos-persona  @anyvm        deny
## (Pasting INTO the persona is also denied, to stop accidental cross-contamination.)
qubes.ClipboardPaste  *  @anyvm               @tag:kratos-persona  deny

## ---- File copy / move: none in either direction ----
qubes.Filecopy        *  @tag:kratos-persona  @anyvm        deny
qubes.Filecopy        *  @anyvm               @tag:kratos-persona  deny

## ---- "Open in VM" / "Open URL": a persona qube can't hand files or links out ----
qubes.OpenInVM        *  @tag:kratos-persona  @anyvm        deny
qubes.OpenURL         *  @tag:kratos-persona  @anyvm        deny
qubes.OpenInVM        *  @anyvm               @tag:kratos-persona  deny
qubes.OpenURL         *  @anyvm               @tag:kratos-persona  deny

## ---- No inter-qube RPC / admin from or to the persona ----
qubes.VMShell         *  @tag:kratos-persona  @anyvm        deny
qubes.VMRootShell     *  @tag:kratos-persona  @anyvm        deny
admin.vm.*            *  @tag:kratos-persona  @anyvm        deny

## ---- Updates for the persona go ONLY through the Whonix updates proxy ----
qubes.UpdatesProxy    *  @tag:kratos-persona  @default      allow target=sys-whonix
